## ** ENCENDER CELERY**

📌 Abrir otra ventana de PowerShell (no cerrar el backend)

### **Paso 1** — Ir al backend

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\GrupoSoluciones\Desktop\Carpeta respaldo\Respaldo\econfia-backend"
```

### **Paso 2** — Activar entorno virtual

```powershell
venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### **Paso 3** — Ejecutar Celery

```powershell
# NO levantar un worker genérico sin -Q, porque consume todas las colas.

# Worker Essential / pipeline clásico
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q essential --pool=threads --concurrency=4 -n essential@%h

# Worker normal / legacy (solo tareas no ruteadas explícitamente)
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q legacy --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n legacy@%h

# Worker de PDF
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q pdf --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n pdf@%h

# Workers FULL (con captura) — completamente separados de Essential
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_1 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full1@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_2 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full2@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_3 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full3@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_4 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full4@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_5 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full5@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_6 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full6@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_7 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full7@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_8 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full8@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_9 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full9@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_10 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full10@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_11 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full11@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q full_12 --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n full12@%h

# Si vas a usar FASK, levanta también sus colas dedicadas
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_fast --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_fast@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_slow --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_slow@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_slow_heavy --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_slow_heavy@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_medio --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_medio@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_medio_heavy --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_medio_heavy@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_mega --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_mega@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_ultra --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_ultra@%h
celery -A backend worker -l info -Q fask_ultra_heavy --pool=solo --concurrency=1 -n fask_ultra_heavy@%h
```

